{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GEtHS1xsSh2yqR1d6cgLU9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the directory exists and contains the expected files. Now I'll write the complete LaTeX paper. Let me carefully construct it based on all the experiment data.\n\nLet me structure the paper for EMNLP 2026 (8 pages main text):\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction (with contributions list)\n3. Related Work\n4. Background: IRT and Person-Fit\n5. IRT-FIT Framework\n6. Experiments\n   6.1 Simulation Study (Exp 1: Inverted-U + Exp 4: Power Theory)\n   6.2 Controlled Contamination (Exp 2+3: Pilot + Full)\n   6.3 Post-RL Robustness (Exp 8)\n   6.4 Baseline Comparison (Exp 7)\n   6.5 Leaderboard-Wide Audit (Exp 5+6)\n7. Discussion (includes domain analysis briefly)\n8. Conclusion\n9. Appendix sections covering the 4PL vs 3PL ablation, multiscale analysis, extended benchmark results, domain-level analysis, and supplementary materials\n\nNow I'm pulling together the key empirical findings to ground the narrative. I have the MMLU power metric at 0.979, AUROC values around 0.93-0.94 across the models I tested, effect sizes in the 2.5-2.8 range for Cohen's d, and the inverted-U pattern peaks around 72% for MMLU and 68% for HellaSwag. The leaderboard audit covers 1847 models with about 12% flagged overall, and I'm tracking the temporal trend showing a 6% baseline that's been shifting.\n\nFor the post-RL analysis, I'm seeing that IRT-FIT maintains strong performance with 94% retention while Min-K%++ drops more substantially. Gemini-1.5 stands out as an extreme case at the 99.8th percentile. I need to reconcile the Gemini lz* values—the framing shows 34.75 but the domain-level breakdown gives me 36.2, 33.8, 30.1, and 28.4, so I should clarify which representation makes most sense for the paper. The percentile ranking shows Gemini sits at 99.8, which is striking given that the mean lz* for unflagged models hovers around 16.8 while flagged ones drop to -12.4—Gemini's highly positive value suggests potential over-consistency or full contamination. Now I'm ready to draft the paper using a straightforward LaTeX article setup that will compile without issues.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5458,"cache_read_input_tokens":45448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5458},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2fd073c-00f4-46f6-847d-2e07ae6f31b5","uuid":"84141c13-6bd9-4d6e-92a3-10b05d04378c"}
